{
  "_about": "Enemies. kind: turret (stands still), floater (hovers and circles at a range), walker (walks after you), moth (flies straight at you and bursts), boss. hp in health points, radius_cm the body, hover_cm the height it floats at, speed_cms, range_cm the distance it keeps, contact the damage of touching it. attacks are tried in order: pattern (patterns.json), windup_ms the glow before it fires, rest_ms after. A boss has phases instead, each starting when its health falls to from_pct. kind blinker: hovers, and as each rest ends reappears elsewhere in sight of you. kind burrower: under the floor between attacks, where it cannot be hurt. burst: a pattern fired once where it dies. zone: the zone whose Codex page lists it. kind agent (zone three): a person who walks the floors and stairs and works with its squad by role: rifle, flank, sniper, shield, grenadier, rush, command, chief (crates/core/src/squad.rs). armour_deg: shots from within this many degrees of its facing glance off. An attack's lock_ms stops its aim following you that long before it fires; indirect needs no line of sight. summon, summon_ms, summon_cap: what it calls, how often, how many of its own at most; rally_pct and rally: a larger call, once, at that health. elite: a bar of its own. kind tank (the Executor): phases list weak (the weak points to break, on the hull or the turret, at_cm in that part's frame: x right, y up, z forward; radius_cm, hp) and cannons (grown in that phase and kept, yaw_deg and pitch_deg off the part's facing); an attack with cannons: true fires from every cannon grown so far, else from the main gun. Its last phase has survive_ms instead of weak points: outlast it. hp is the weak points' total.",
